# .gitleaksignore — suppress ONE specific finding by its fingerprint.
#
# Fingerprint format:  <commit-sha>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>
# Get it from the "Fingerprint:" line in `gitleaks git -v` output, or the
# "Fingerprint" field of the JSON report.
#
# Why fingerprints and not path globs? A fingerprint pins the exact commit +
# line. If someone later adds a REAL key to the same file, it still gets
# caught. A path allowlist would hide it forever.
#
# Every entry needs: who, when, why. Review this file in every PR.
#
# Example (replace with a fingerprint from YOUR sandbox scan):
# 2025-01-15 alice  AWS docs example key in parser test fixture, not a credential
# 3f2a1b9c0d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0a9b8c7d6e5f4a:tests/test_config.py:aws-access-token:2
